 <longdesc><para unique="1048995">This instruction loads one FP16 element from memory, converts it to FP32, and broadcasts it to a SIMD register.</para>
  <para unique="1048996">This instruction does not generate floating-point exceptions and does not consult or update MXCSR. </para>
  <para unique="1048997">Input FP16 denormals are converted to normal FP32 numbers and not treated as zero. Since any FP16 number can be represented in FP32, the conversion result is exact and no rounding is needed.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1048999">VBCSTNESH2PS dest, src (VEX encoded version)</title>
   <programlisting>VL = (128, 256)
KL = VL/32
FOR i in range(0, KL):
	tmp.dword[i].word[0] = src.word[0] // read 16b from memory
FOR i in range(0, KL):
	dest.dword[i] = convert_fp16_to_fp32(tmp.dword[i].word[0]) 																		//SAE
DEST[MAXVL-1:VL] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Flags Affected">
  <para unique="1048329">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting>VBCSTNESH2PS __m128 _mm_bcstnesh_ps (const _Float16* __A);
VBCSTNESH2PS __m256 _mm256_bcstnesh_ps (const _Float16* __A);</programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1047135">None.</para>
  </subsection>
